<h2>Count words, characters and reading time</h2><p class="lead">Get live counts while you write or edit.</p><div class="field"><label for="text">Your text</label><textarea id="text" style="min-height:260px" placeholder="Start typing or paste text here…">Clear writing starts with understanding what the reader needs.</textarea></div><div class="result-box"><div class="result-grid"><div class="metric"><span>Words</span><strong id="words">0</strong></div><div class="metric"><span>Characters</span><strong id="chars">0</strong></div><div class="metric"><span>Characters without spaces</span><strong id="nospaces">0</strong></div><div class="metric"><span>Sentences</span><strong id="sentences">0</strong></div><div class="metric"><span>Paragraphs</span><strong id="paragraphs">0</strong></div><div class="metric"><span>Estimated reading time</span><strong id="reading">0 min</strong></div></div></div>
<script>(()=>{const t=document.getElementById('text'),$=i=>document.getElementById(i);function go(){const v=t.value,words=(v.match(/[\p{L}\p{N}]+(?:['’-][\p{L}\p{N}]+)*/gu)||[]),paragraphs=v.trim()?v.trim().split(/\n\s*\n/).filter(Boolean).length:0,sentences=v.trim()?(v.match(/[^.!?]+[.!?]+(?:\s|$)|[^.!?]+$/g)||[]).filter(x=>x.trim()).length:0;$('words').textContent=words.length;$('chars').textContent=v.length;$('nospaces').textContent=v.replace(/\s/g,'').length;$('sentences').textContent=sentences;$('paragraphs').textContent=paragraphs;$('reading').textContent=words.length?Math.max(1,Math.ceil(words.length/220))+' min':'0 min'}t.addEventListener('input',go);go()})();</script>
<?php $toolBody=ob_get_clean();ob_start(); ?>
<h2>What this counter measures</h2><p>The tool reports words, all characters, characters excluding whitespace, approximate sentence count, paragraph count and an estimated reading time based on 220 words per minute.</p><h2>How word counting works</h2><p>Words are detected using letters and numbers with support for common apostrophes and hyphens inside terms. Different editors can count edge cases differently, so expect small differences for unusual punctuation or formatting.</p><h2>Reading time is an estimate</h2><p>Actual reading speed depends on language, complexity, reader familiarity and purpose. The reading-time figure is a planning aid, not a measurement of how long every person will take.</p><h2>Useful ways to apply the counts</h2><p>Writers can check platform limits, editors can spot unexpectedly long sections, and content teams can estimate reading burden before publication.</p>
